  "markscheme": {
    "html": "<section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"a.i\"><p><strong>a.i</strong></p><p>equally spaced arrows «by eye» all pointing down ✓ edge effects also shown with arrows ✓</p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"a.ii\"><p><strong>a.ii</strong></p><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"E=\\frac{V}{d}=\\frac{960}{8.0\\times 10^{-3}}\"></span> ✓ <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"E=1.2\\times 10^{5}\"></span> «NC<sup>−1</sup>» ✓</p>\n<p>In an experiment, an oil drop is introduced into the space between the plates through a small hole in the upper plate. The oil drop moves through air in a tube before falling between the plates.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_03\"><img alt=\"Source markscheme diagram 3\" src=\"asset:fig_03\"/></figure></p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"b\"><p><strong>b</strong></p><p>friction transfers electron(s) to or from drop AND through collisions/ interaction with air molecules in the tube OR through collisions/interaction with wall of tube ✓</p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"c.i\"><p><strong>c.i</strong></p><p>weight of oil drop is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\rho_{o}gV\"></span> ✓ <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{F_{b}}{W}=\\frac{\\rho_{a}gV}{\\rho_{o}gV}=\\frac{\\rho_{a}}{\\rho_{o}}\"></span> ✓   «<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{F_{b}}{W}=\\frac{1}{730}=\"></span>» <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1.4\\times 10^{-3}\"></span> OR Ratio of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F_{b}\"></span> to <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"W\"></span> is much less than 1 ✓</p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"c.ii\"><p><strong>c.ii</strong></p><p>Weight vertically down AND electric force vertically up ✓ Of equal length «by eye» ✓</p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"c.iii\"><p><strong>c.iii</strong></p><p>Mass of drop is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\rho_{o}V\"></span> ✓ <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"qE=\\rho_{o}Vg\"></span> ✓ «hence answer»<br/>MP1 must be shown implicitly for credit.</p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"c.iv\"><p><strong>c.iv</strong></p><p>Negative ✓</p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"d.i\"><p><strong>d.i</strong></p><p>Net force is zero ✓ Acceleration of the oil drop is zero ✓ OR For terminal velocity drag must equal weight weight <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"=\\rho_{o}gV\"></span> and drag <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"=6\\piηrv\"></span> ✓</p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"d.ii\"><p><strong>d.ii</strong></p><p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"q=\\frac{6\\piηrv}{E}\"></span> ✓ <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"q=\\frac{6\\pi\\times 1.60\\times 10^{-5}\\times 1.36\\times 10^{-6}\\times 1.40\\times 10^{-4}}{1.2\\times 10^{5}}\"></span> ✓ <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"q=4.79\\times 10^{-19}\"></span> «C» ✓ Answer must be shown to 3+ sf.</p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"d.iii\"><p><strong>d.iii</strong></p><p>charge is quantized ✓ so, the charges must be 1e and 2e ✓</p></section>"
